@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-item_group a ds:Subcomponent;
    ds:name "SideNavigation.ItemGroup";
    ds:summary "A navigation item group organises related navigation items into a section within the primary or secondary navigation. Each group can have an optional group header and is separated from the previous group by a divider.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "SideNavigation.ItemGroup\n├── Divider (shown before every group except the first)\n├── Group header (optional)\n└── Navigation item (repeatable)\n```\n\n```\n---\n# SideNavigation.ItemGroup — a group of navigation items with an optional\n# header.\n#\n# Authored 2026-10-16 from the supplied planning tree ALONE. No\n# implementation was read, so this anatomy carries STRUCTURE ONLY.\n#\n# The tree marks the divider \"shown before every group except the first\".\n# That is a property of the group's POSITION AMONG ITS SIBLINGS, which a\n# node cannot see from inside its own anatomy. It is modelled here as an\n# optional leading node; the rule that decides when it appears belongs to\n# the parent that lays the groups out.\nnode:\n  uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-item_group\n  edges:\n    # Absent on the first group of a Nav.\n    - node:\n        role: divider\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n    - node:\n        uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-group_header\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n        slotName: header\n    - node:\n        uri: apps.subcomponent.side_navigation-item\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1..*\"\n        slotName: default";
    ds:anatomyClassic "Primary navigation item group anatomy\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=10063-14072&t=HfRgpBcYWYYrZVn8-1\n\nPrimary navigation item group styling\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=10064-25394&t=HfRgpBcYWYYrZVn8-1\n\nSecondary navigation item group anatomy\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=10063-14563&t=HfRgpBcYWYYrZVn8-1\n\nSecondary navigation item group styling\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=10064-25561&t=HfRgpBcYWYYrZVn8-1";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\nUse navigation item groups to organise navigation items into different sections. Group headers can be used to describe the category that the items in each group belong to.\n\n### When not to use\n\nAvoid creating separate groups when navigation items belong to the same section.";
    ds:guidelines "## Content specification\n\n### Group header\n\nEach group can have an optional group header. The group header describes the category that the navigation items in the group belong to.\n\nGroup headers are displayed on a single line and truncated when there is insufficient space. When text is truncated, a tooltip displaying the full text appears after an 800 ms hover delay.\n\n### Divider\n\nEach group, except the first, should have a divider at the top to separate it from the previous group.\n\n### Navigation items\n\nA navigation item group can contain multiple navigation items.\n\nIn primary navigation, items can be expandable, opening their children inline, or open secondary navigation. Within each group, navigation items should either all have icons or none should.\n\nIn secondary navigation, navigation items cannot have icons or be expandable.\n\n## Responsive behaviour\n\nNavigation item groups follow the responsive behaviour defined in the main Side navigation documentation.\n\n## Accessibility\n\n### Keyboard navigation\n\nNavigation items within each group should follow a logical, top-to-bottom focus order.\n\n### Screen reader\n\nNavigation groups should be announced as navigation sections:\n\n- Start of group: Announced as the start of a navigation section.\n- Group header: Announced as a group heading followed by its label.\n- End of group: Announced as the end of the group.";
    ds:tier ds:apps;
    ds:parentComponent ds:apps.component.side_navigation.
